<h1>Daniel Edward Maloney</h1>
<p>Judge up for retention, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Incumbent.</p>
<p>Circuit Court of Cook County</p>
<h2>Ratings</h2>
<ul>
<li>Chicago Bar Association: <a href="https://www.chicagobar.org/votejudges#:~:text=Daniel%20Edward%20Maloney" rel="nofollow noopener">Qualified</a></li>
<li>Illinois State Bar Association: <a href="https://www.isba.org/judicial-elections/counties/cook#:~:text=Daniel%20Edward%20Maloney" rel="nofollow noopener">Yes</a></li>
<li>Injustice Watch: <a href="https://2026retention.injusticewatch.org/candidate/daniel-edward-maloney-35835" rel="nofollow noopener">Former prosecutor</a></li>
</ul>
<h2>Record</h2>
<p>Appointed to the Circuit Court in 2019 and elected in 2020; handles felony preliminary hearings at the Markham courthouse and presides over three specialty courts for veterans and people with substance abuse or mental health problems. A judge stays on the bench with a yes from 60 percent of voters.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Division counsel at the Drug Enforcement Administration&#39;s regional field office (2017-2019); Cook County assistant state&#39;s attorney, including eight years in the narcotics unit (2001-2017). Law degree from Valparaiso University (2001).</p>
